1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,440
Do you think you two could stop snarling at each other every time you meet?

2
00:00:09,580 --> 00:00:12,220
She's the one who's always glaring at me, rude!

3
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:14,640
Because you need to appreciate fried tofu fritters!

4
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:18,100
I suppose if you've been trying to kill each other since the moment you've met,

5
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:19,780
then there's nothing I can do.

6
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:24,040
Huh? No, I wouldn't say we always wanted to kill each other, right?

7
00:00:24,380 --> 00:00:26,900
Yeah, I agree. That part came much later.

8
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:28,820
Okay, enlighten me.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Thank you.

10
00:02:03,947 --> 00:02:08,687
I heard there might be a civil war soon

11
00:02:08,687 --> 00:02:10,487
Looks like it

12
00:02:10,487 --> 00:02:13,947
The royal succession dispute is finally coming to a head

13
00:02:13,947 --> 00:02:17,547
At this rate, the neighboring country is going to capitalize on it

14
00:02:17,547 --> 00:02:20,127
Humans are such foolish creatures

15
00:02:20,127 --> 00:02:23,387
Every time they open their mouths, it's about conflict

16
00:02:23,387 --> 00:02:26,507
They don't even try to enjoy their worthless lives

17
00:02:26,507 --> 00:02:28,827
The priestess of the Holy Seas is here

18
00:02:28,827 --> 00:02:30,487
Wait, the priestess?

19
00:02:30,627 --> 00:02:33,287
What a miracle for her to finally come to our town

20
00:02:33,287 --> 00:02:36,727
Thank goodness, she's come to save us at last

21
00:02:36,727 --> 00:02:39,027
The priestess of the Holy Seas

22
00:02:39,027 --> 00:02:41,527
She intervenes in human conflicts

23
00:02:41,527 --> 00:02:43,967
And creates favorable resolutions

24
00:02:43,967 --> 00:02:47,407
If the conflict is over water or food

25
00:02:47,407 --> 00:02:49,887
She creates lakes and abundant harvests

26
00:02:49,887 --> 00:02:54,387
If humans clash, she uses her power to make them lose their will to fight

27
00:02:54,387 --> 00:02:56,287
She must be a god

28
00:02:56,287 --> 00:02:58,767
Or a similar type of entity at least

29
00:02:58,767 --> 00:03:03,247
Either way, it's against the rules for such beings to interfere in human society

30
00:03:03,247 --> 00:03:08,187
That must be her

31
00:03:08,187 --> 00:03:09,347
What's she like?

32
00:03:22,407 --> 00:03:23,407
That woman?

33
00:03:23,907 --> 00:03:26,247
She's neither a god nor a divine messenger

34
00:03:26,247 --> 00:03:27,247
Is she...

35
00:03:27,247 --> 00:03:29,527
Does she think this is a joke?

36
00:03:35,187 --> 00:03:40,567
What are you doing?

37
00:03:41,207 --> 00:03:43,307
Honestly, a dragon-turned priestess?

38
00:03:43,987 --> 00:03:45,387
And they believe you?

39
00:03:45,627 --> 00:03:47,367
I could ask you the very same thing

40
00:03:47,367 --> 00:03:51,107
Why is the Emperor of Demise's daughter living amongst humans?

41
00:03:52,707 --> 00:03:55,527
If I remember correctly, you're called Toru, right?

42
00:03:56,187 --> 00:03:59,747
And if you must know, I don't believe human beings should be fighting each other

43
00:03:59,747 --> 00:04:02,827
It is foolish to sacrifice unnecessary blood

44
00:04:02,827 --> 00:04:05,987
I have the power to stop that, so I do

45
00:04:05,987 --> 00:04:10,267
Are you saying there are Harmony Dragons that exist who will actually do some work?

46
00:04:11,767 --> 00:04:14,947
I bet you've had quite a few human sacrifices offered up

47
00:04:14,947 --> 00:04:17,687
It doesn't matter, I don't need human sacrifices

48
00:04:17,687 --> 00:04:18,727
You don't?

49
00:04:19,187 --> 00:04:19,747
Why not?

50
00:04:20,127 --> 00:04:21,707
Who would ever want to eat a human?

51
00:04:21,707 --> 00:04:23,107
I don't believe they're tasty

52
00:04:23,107 --> 00:04:27,607
I'm willing to bet there are much more delicious things in this world

53
00:04:27,607 --> 00:04:30,947
And it is my belief that humans will be the ones to create them

54
00:04:30,947 --> 00:04:33,367
I see

55
00:04:33,367 --> 00:04:35,887
She's the oddball Quetzalcoatl mentioned

56
00:04:35,887 --> 00:04:37,487
You must be Elma, then?

57
00:04:38,327 --> 00:04:38,807
Nice

58
00:04:38,807 --> 00:04:40,767
What food do you usually exchange?

59
00:04:41,527 --> 00:04:45,147
Are you absolutely sure you don't belong to the Chaos faction?

60
00:04:45,647 --> 00:04:48,747
Speaking of oddballs, you're not exactly typical either

61
00:04:48,747 --> 00:04:52,047
I've never met a Chaos dragon who wasn't looking for chaos

62
00:04:52,047 --> 00:04:54,747
None are ever willing to engage in conversation

63
00:04:54,747 --> 00:05:00,167
Well, before I eliminated you, I wanted to do some investigating

64
00:05:00,167 --> 00:05:02,407
Investigating? Huh

65
00:05:02,407 --> 00:05:06,347
Would you care to join me for a while and further your education?

66
00:05:06,707 --> 00:05:07,107
Where?

67
00:05:08,687 --> 00:05:10,067
Here in the world of humans

68
00:05:10,067 --> 00:05:12,347
We can investigate together

69
00:05:12,347 --> 00:05:18,027
So you two traveled together for a while, then?

70
00:05:18,027 --> 00:05:19,907
Yeah, I guess

71
00:05:19,907 --> 00:05:23,367
I put up with her self-righteous act for too long

72
00:05:23,367 --> 00:05:26,207
I truly don't know what I was thinking, Kobayashi

73
00:05:26,207 --> 00:05:29,387
Sounds to me like you were both just feeling each other out

74
00:05:29,387 --> 00:05:31,787
Trying way too hard to get along

75
00:05:31,787 --> 00:05:34,127
When you had very different values

76
00:05:34,127 --> 00:05:37,827
Yeah, I guess that sounds about right

77
00:05:37,827 --> 00:05:41,147
I was more interested in getting to know Elma personally

78
00:05:41,147 --> 00:05:45,087
She had so much freedom and always seemed to be doing exactly what she wanted

79
00:05:45,087 --> 00:05:48,587
I know it's been a while, but that's the way I remember it

80
00:05:48,587 --> 00:05:49,207
Mm-hmm

81
00:05:49,207 --> 00:05:50,687
Okay, so then what?

82
00:05:50,827 --> 00:05:51,787
Oh, right, sorry

83
00:05:51,787 --> 00:05:54,427
We came to understand one another somehow

84
00:05:54,427 --> 00:05:56,247
We accepted that we'll never agree

85
00:05:56,247 --> 00:05:58,147
That's why it made sense

86
00:05:58,147 --> 00:05:59,387
To kill each other

87
00:05:59,387 --> 00:05:59,927
Hmm

88
00:05:59,927 --> 00:06:02,387
That makes no sense at all

89
00:06:02,387 --> 00:06:11,227
Why, Toru?

90
00:06:11,507 --> 00:06:13,787
What possessed you to destroy the palace?

91
00:06:14,127 --> 00:06:16,927
Don't you understand that was supposed to be a symbol of peace?

92
00:06:17,627 --> 00:06:18,467
Was it?

93
00:06:18,987 --> 00:06:22,547
The thought of peace requiring your presence gave me chills

94
00:06:22,547 --> 00:06:23,127
What?

95
00:06:23,967 --> 00:06:26,367
This palace was erected for you

96
00:06:26,367 --> 00:06:29,767
A place for people to come and worship you as a god

97
00:06:29,767 --> 00:06:36,727
And from this origin, a religion centered around you took root and adopted a class-based society full of inequality

98
00:06:36,727 --> 00:06:42,567
In time, there would come to be conflict with those who refused to accept you

99
00:06:42,567 --> 00:06:44,827
I would have forbidden that!

100
00:06:45,487 --> 00:06:48,507
You're not listening to what I'm trying to share with you

101
00:06:48,507 --> 00:06:52,587
Tell me, do you intend to remain here with these humans for all eternity?

102
00:06:53,447 --> 00:06:57,547
Granting the desires of others, and acting as a symbol of worship forever?

103
00:06:58,967 --> 00:07:03,507
I'm dying to know if you intended to let yourself get dragged into the human agenda

104
00:07:03,507 --> 00:07:07,907
Or did you foolishly believe you were operating under your own power?

105
00:07:08,507 --> 00:07:10,627
You diverged from your plan, Elma

106
00:07:10,627 --> 00:07:12,487
I'm disappointed in you

107
00:07:12,487 --> 00:07:15,547
I can't stand how disgraceful you've become

108
00:07:15,547 --> 00:07:19,187
I've no choice but to kill you and wake those humans from their dream

109
00:07:19,187 --> 00:07:20,867
If that's what you want

110
00:07:20,867 --> 00:07:22,967
Then come for me, Toru!

111
00:07:23,187 --> 00:07:24,447
Take my life!

112
00:07:28,367 --> 00:07:29,867
I knew this was coming

113
00:07:29,867 --> 00:07:32,027
It was never going in a good direction

114
00:07:32,027 --> 00:07:34,547
But what else was I supposed to do?

115
00:07:34,847 --> 00:07:36,847
They brought me food as compensation

116
00:07:36,847 --> 00:07:39,647
I couldn't resist, and it was delicious!

117
00:07:39,647 --> 00:07:39,927
I'm not going to be able to do it

118
00:07:39,927 --> 00:07:40,547
I'm not going to be able to do it

119
00:07:40,547 --> 00:07:41,547
I'm not going to be able to do it

120
00:07:41,547 --> 00:07:42,547
I'm not going to be able to do it

121
00:07:42,547 --> 00:07:43,547
I'm not going to be able to do it

122
00:07:43,547 --> 00:07:44,547
I'm not going to be able to do it

123
00:07:44,547 --> 00:07:47,187
She's...

124
00:07:47,187 --> 00:07:51,647
She's so, so strong!

125
00:07:51,647 --> 00:08:13,667
And that was it

126
00:08:13,667 --> 00:08:16,047
That was how we severed ties conclusively

127
00:08:16,047 --> 00:08:17,547
Hmm...

128
00:08:17,547 --> 00:08:20,327
That sounds simultaneously grandiose and petty

129
00:08:20,327 --> 00:08:23,467
And in the end, I returned to the Harmony Faction's base

130
00:08:23,467 --> 00:08:24,507
And I guess that was that

131
00:08:24,507 --> 00:08:26,707
I never got involved with humans again

132
00:08:26,707 --> 00:08:29,927
So you fight now because you two get along so well

133
00:08:29,927 --> 00:08:31,867
What do you mean?

134
00:08:31,927 --> 00:08:33,567
Did you not listen to our story?

135
00:08:33,767 --> 00:08:34,887
No, we don't get along!

136
00:08:34,967 --> 00:08:36,327
We're completely at odds with each other!

137
00:08:36,807 --> 00:08:37,767
I couldn't tell

138
00:08:37,767 --> 00:08:40,247
Toru's been uncharacteristically chill

139
00:08:40,247 --> 00:08:42,547
And you always seem to have your hands too full

140
00:08:42,547 --> 00:08:44,027
With work to try to lead humanity

141
00:08:44,027 --> 00:08:47,927
So, wouldn't that mean you don't really have a reason to fight in this world?

142
00:08:48,207 --> 00:08:48,607
What?

143
00:08:50,007 --> 00:08:51,467
Come on, Ms. Kobayashi

144
00:08:51,467 --> 00:08:54,087
Do you not understand why things are like that here?

145
00:08:54,327 --> 00:08:54,707
What?

146
00:08:55,247 --> 00:08:57,307
It's because the food here is irresistible

147
00:08:57,307 --> 00:08:59,607
And both Toru and I have a gluttonous streak

148
00:08:59,607 --> 00:09:01,987
I'll never be anything like you!

149
00:09:01,987 --> 00:09:02,707
What do you mean?

150
00:09:03,327 --> 00:09:05,107
You're way too easily enticed by food!

151
00:09:05,227 --> 00:09:05,647
I'm not!

152
00:09:05,787 --> 00:09:08,887
Please, tasting human culture is the best way to understand humans!

153
00:09:09,247 --> 00:09:11,687
You'll make up any excuse to stop your stupid face!

154
00:09:11,927 --> 00:09:14,187
As if you're not totally booked on human food yourself

155
00:09:14,187 --> 00:09:15,287
Day after day, you're cooking

156
00:09:15,287 --> 00:09:17,987
They've become so close, they understand each other's thoughts

157
00:09:17,987 --> 00:09:21,807
Then they fight to shave away the parts they still can't accept

158
00:09:21,807 --> 00:09:24,427
Trying to compare it to your unnatural appearance

159
00:09:24,427 --> 00:09:26,627
I've always wanted to have friends like that myself

160
00:09:26,627 --> 00:09:28,147
I don't even know what natural means!

161
00:09:56,627 --> 00:09:58,127
You don't know what natural means!

162
00:09:58,127 --> 00:09:58,967
Things are like that.

163
00:09:58,967 --> 00:09:59,847
非常的 status

164
00:09:59,847 --> 00:10:01,507
There's always reasons why individuals eat the chicken

165
00:10:01,507 --> 00:10:02,227
To be honest human beings

166
00:10:02,227 --> 00:10:04,947
We look at the 안ie

167
00:10:04,947 --> 00:10:06,847
To be honest human being

168
00:10:07,847 --> 00:10:08,847
The reason why they say??

169
00:10:24,367 --> 00:10:25,087
Love you to Alaska

170
00:10:25,087 --> 00:10:36,207
I'm going to kill you, E-Lulu.

171
00:10:37,907 --> 00:10:39,807
All you do around here is sleep!

172
00:10:40,107 --> 00:10:42,027
You need to go out there and get a job!

173
00:10:42,187 --> 00:10:44,347
I promise I've been thinking about my future.

174
00:10:44,807 --> 00:10:45,507
One more century...

175
00:10:45,507 --> 00:10:47,087
You're not on Dragon Time anymore!

176
00:10:48,667 --> 00:10:50,127
Oh, that's right, I forgot.

177
00:10:50,767 --> 00:10:52,307
I'll help you with your work for now.

178
00:10:52,307 --> 00:10:53,747
You take that back!

179
00:10:53,927 --> 00:10:55,807
As if you could ever handle the work of a maid!

180
00:10:55,907 --> 00:10:58,487
Do not underestimate me or I'll be forced to prove you wrong!

181
00:10:58,747 --> 00:11:00,887
Isn't that what Kobayashi is always saying to you?

182
00:11:01,947 --> 00:11:03,767
Wait, this work you speak of.

183
00:11:04,047 --> 00:11:05,367
Does Kobayashi do that?

184
00:11:05,567 --> 00:11:06,567
Yes, she does.

185
00:11:06,727 --> 00:11:08,887
And now she works harder so that you can eat too.

186
00:11:09,627 --> 00:11:10,887
Then I guess I can work.

187
00:11:11,347 --> 00:11:13,307
I want to work with Kobayashi's place, though.

188
00:11:13,327 --> 00:11:14,647
I'll erase your existence!

189
00:11:15,047 --> 00:11:16,967
You're scaring me. Please stop!

190
00:11:17,047 --> 00:11:18,227
And I'll melt her, Mom!

191
00:11:18,267 --> 00:11:19,607
What does Emma have to do with this?

192
00:11:19,607 --> 00:11:23,267
If you're trying to preserve your laziness,

193
00:11:23,387 --> 00:11:25,787
there are ways you can search for a job without leaving our house.

194
00:11:25,907 --> 00:11:26,507
Use the computer.

195
00:11:27,007 --> 00:11:27,667
No, thanks.

196
00:11:28,147 --> 00:11:30,367
I'd rather go out and test the jobs myself.

197
00:11:32,347 --> 00:11:33,587
Shall we go look around?

198
00:11:33,987 --> 00:11:36,027
It's my first time passing through here.

199
00:11:36,347 --> 00:11:38,407
I've flown over to the roof several times, though.

200
00:11:38,747 --> 00:11:40,167
You're kind of like a cat.

201
00:11:40,567 --> 00:11:43,187
Are you sure you wouldn't be better off living in the wild?

202
00:11:43,707 --> 00:11:44,427
Oh, fine.

203
00:11:44,427 --> 00:11:47,087
I should admit you have been putting in some effort.

204
00:11:47,967 --> 00:11:50,007
You learned perception blocking, which is challenging.

205
00:11:50,507 --> 00:11:52,867
And you managed to form proper hands, which I appreciate.

206
00:11:53,887 --> 00:11:55,067
You've worked very hard.

207
00:11:55,907 --> 00:11:57,767
I kind of like when you're nice to me.

208
00:11:58,387 --> 00:11:59,207
I like you.

209
00:12:00,187 --> 00:12:01,767
You shouldn't get so personal.

210
00:12:02,567 --> 00:12:03,007
Fine.

211
00:12:03,307 --> 00:12:04,847
I still like Kobayashi more.

212
00:12:05,007 --> 00:12:05,627
You would.

213
00:12:06,087 --> 00:12:06,667
Nothing yet?

214
00:12:06,747 --> 00:12:08,907
I can't believe you haven't seen anything you'd want to try.

215
00:12:08,907 --> 00:12:15,007
I can't do anything with meat and fish without wanting to devour them.

216
00:12:15,247 --> 00:12:16,587
Spoken like a true chaos dragon.

217
00:12:16,747 --> 00:12:18,327
Flowers make me want to trample them.

218
00:12:18,607 --> 00:12:19,127
It's true.

219
00:12:19,247 --> 00:12:20,167
We were born to destroy.

220
00:12:20,427 --> 00:12:21,827
Books make me want to burn them.

221
00:12:22,107 --> 00:12:23,647
Classic chaos dragon trait.

222
00:12:24,147 --> 00:12:25,887
Unfortunately, all those things are forbidden.

223
00:12:26,687 --> 00:12:27,547
Yeah, I know.

224
00:12:28,307 --> 00:12:30,827
It's so hard having to ignore those instincts, though.

225
00:12:30,867 --> 00:12:33,887
On the flip side, we wouldn't be here if we weren't able to deny them.

226
00:12:34,427 --> 00:12:35,627
You know how to do that?

227
00:12:35,987 --> 00:12:37,187
Of course I do.

228
00:12:37,187 --> 00:12:40,507
But, um, I guess that means there's nowhere here you can work.

229
00:12:40,527 --> 00:12:40,887
Hey!

230
00:12:41,327 --> 00:12:42,127
Let's play!

231
00:12:43,067 --> 00:12:44,727
Okay, let's play!

232
00:12:44,867 --> 00:12:46,047
Do you want to come with us?

233
00:12:46,287 --> 00:12:47,147
Where are you going?

234
00:12:48,107 --> 00:12:48,507
Shopping!

235
00:12:48,727 --> 00:12:49,627
Yeah, sure!

236
00:12:49,727 --> 00:12:50,587
Let's go this way.

237
00:12:52,467 --> 00:12:52,907
Yes!

238
00:12:53,587 --> 00:12:54,227
Yoo-hoo!

239
00:12:54,567 --> 00:12:55,267
Hi, Kana!

240
00:12:55,427 --> 00:12:56,147
Hi, Saikawa!

241
00:12:56,407 --> 00:12:57,347
Oh, you're here!

242
00:12:57,607 --> 00:12:58,647
Hi, Lady Toru.

243
00:12:58,787 --> 00:12:59,587
Hi, Elulu.

244
00:12:59,887 --> 00:13:00,547
Yeah, hi!

245
00:13:00,747 --> 00:13:02,007
What are you guys doing here?

246
00:13:02,067 --> 00:13:03,247
That's what I want to know.

247
00:13:03,407 --> 00:13:03,707
Kana?

248
00:13:04,387 --> 00:13:06,687
This is just where we hang out sometimes.

249
00:13:06,687 --> 00:13:08,747
Are these ladies friends of yours, Kana?

250
00:13:08,867 --> 00:13:10,447
They seem very pretty and nice.

251
00:13:10,607 --> 00:13:11,647
My name's Toru.

252
00:13:11,887 --> 00:13:12,707
This is Elulu.

253
00:13:13,367 --> 00:13:15,687
We were searching for a part-time job for her, but...

254
00:13:18,287 --> 00:13:21,287
Which one should we get?

255
00:13:21,627 --> 00:13:22,267
Who cares?

256
00:13:22,387 --> 00:13:23,227
They all taste great.

257
00:13:23,727 --> 00:13:24,207
Yes!

258
00:13:24,407 --> 00:13:26,347
Kana, this would look so good on you!

259
00:13:26,567 --> 00:13:27,767
Try this one, Saikawa.

260
00:13:27,767 --> 00:13:33,047
I have a yellow one.

261
00:13:35,047 --> 00:13:37,027
I haven't seen you here before.

262
00:13:37,627 --> 00:13:38,987
Are you the maid's little sister?

263
00:13:39,627 --> 00:13:42,007
Wow, you have such an adorable shop, Miss Saida.

264
00:13:42,727 --> 00:13:44,027
Elulu, this is Miss Saida.

265
00:13:44,127 --> 00:13:45,387
Miss Saida, this is Elulu.

266
00:13:45,567 --> 00:13:47,947
We see each other at the neighborhood association meetings.

267
00:13:48,607 --> 00:13:49,067
Oh, no!

268
00:13:49,747 --> 00:13:51,247
What happened to your poor leg?

269
00:13:51,247 --> 00:13:53,587
I messed it up while jogging this morning.

270
00:13:53,807 --> 00:13:57,467
I'm getting old, so I've been thinking of closing up shop one of these days.

271
00:13:57,607 --> 00:13:57,927
No!

272
00:13:59,927 --> 00:14:02,827
But as you can see, I don't think I can.

273
00:14:04,507 --> 00:14:06,287
There are a lot of kids here.

274
00:14:06,807 --> 00:14:11,527
Because we're a dogashi shop, many different children have been coming here for decades now

275
00:14:11,527 --> 00:14:12,907
to get their favorite treat.

276
00:14:13,127 --> 00:14:14,687
Could I work at the shop with you?

277
00:14:15,647 --> 00:14:16,587
I don't know.

278
00:14:16,707 --> 00:14:17,567
How old are you?

279
00:14:17,887 --> 00:14:19,407
She's the same age as I am.

280
00:14:19,907 --> 00:14:20,927
The same as you?

281
00:14:21,507 --> 00:14:22,187
Let's see.

282
00:14:22,507 --> 00:14:23,727
I'm not sure what to do.

283
00:14:24,447 --> 00:14:27,187
I was thinking my grandson would run the shop after me.

284
00:14:27,647 --> 00:14:31,907
But it might be better to have someone enthusiastic about it instead of someone reluctant.

285
00:14:32,367 --> 00:14:33,527
I would recommend her.

286
00:14:36,467 --> 00:14:36,947
Huh?

287
00:14:38,367 --> 00:14:38,847
Oh!

288
00:14:38,847 --> 00:14:47,627
Okay.

289
00:14:48,627 --> 00:14:49,027
Wow.

290
00:14:49,367 --> 00:14:51,247
You're working part-time at a dogashi shop?

291
00:14:51,627 --> 00:14:53,127
It's the Obero shop.

292
00:14:53,467 --> 00:14:54,947
Have you heard of it, Kobayashi?

293
00:14:55,167 --> 00:14:57,727
That's the one at the end of the shopping district, isn't it?

294
00:14:58,027 --> 00:15:02,067
She's forgetting to tell you that she only got hired because I lent her my voice of authority.

295
00:15:02,547 --> 00:15:03,207
It's true.

296
00:15:03,207 --> 00:15:06,247
She was firm when commanding her emotions, and I thought she was terrifying.

297
00:15:06,347 --> 00:15:07,527
I need more praise, please.

298
00:15:07,527 --> 00:15:09,147
I don't know that that was praise.

299
00:15:12,727 --> 00:15:14,927
Will it be okay, the job?

300
00:15:16,967 --> 00:15:17,807
You're worried?

301
00:15:18,927 --> 00:15:21,267
You chose it because you're interested in it, right?

302
00:15:22,747 --> 00:15:23,147
Mm-hmm.

303
00:15:29,147 --> 00:15:32,927
When I started my job, I didn't think much about it until much later either.

304
00:15:33,867 --> 00:15:36,427
Eventually, you'll discover things you find fulfilling about it.

305
00:15:37,527 --> 00:15:45,227
I became a maid because I was interested in it, and it's very fulfilling.

306
00:15:45,707 --> 00:15:47,567
So why aren't you betting me?

307
00:15:47,927 --> 00:15:53,027
Elu, make sure you always respect the needs of others and do everything to the best of your ability.

308
00:15:53,787 --> 00:15:55,987
This mage should not be considered a role model.

309
00:15:56,647 --> 00:15:57,047
Rude!

310
00:15:57,107 --> 00:15:58,867
Mizzcomo-yachi!

311
00:16:01,247 --> 00:16:02,347
how-by-

312
00:16:02,347 --> 00:16:04,347
I

313
00:16:32,347 --> 00:16:36,427
Hm? What's wrong, Take?

314
00:16:36,427 --> 00:16:39,307
I feel bad for my grandma. She hurt her leg.

315
00:16:39,607 --> 00:16:41,147
Are you stuck helping out?

316
00:16:41,407 --> 00:16:43,427
No. Apparently she hired someone,

317
00:16:43,527 --> 00:16:45,347
but she wants me to go by and train them for her.

318
00:16:45,967 --> 00:16:49,507
Wow. I'm impressed she agreed to hire someone outside the family.

319
00:16:49,827 --> 00:16:52,487
Yeah. She asked me to bring a uniform over today.

320
00:16:53,027 --> 00:16:54,667
But check it out. It's huge.

321
00:16:55,147 --> 00:16:57,127
I mean, it looks big enough to fit an adult man.

322
00:16:57,347 --> 00:16:59,747
So it bothers you that she hired a guy? That's weird.

323
00:17:00,067 --> 00:17:01,747
I don't know where she could have met this dude.

324
00:17:01,747 --> 00:17:03,447
He better not be some psychopath.

325
00:17:04,247 --> 00:17:05,867
That's Granny's little warrior.

326
00:17:06,267 --> 00:17:06,987
Shut up.

327
00:17:07,967 --> 00:17:10,667
This is weird. What the heck are they like?

328
00:17:11,367 --> 00:17:12,447
Good afternoon.

329
00:17:13,287 --> 00:17:15,687
That's why it's an adult size. Crazy.

330
00:17:17,547 --> 00:17:18,987
Are you Ida's grandson?

331
00:17:19,627 --> 00:17:20,807
I'm Takito, yeah.

332
00:17:21,327 --> 00:17:22,927
I'm Alulu. I'm 16.

333
00:17:23,447 --> 00:17:24,907
That's what I'm supposed to say.

334
00:17:24,927 --> 00:17:28,267
The same age. Your name. Are you a transfer student?

335
00:17:29,027 --> 00:17:30,287
How did you meet my grandma?

336
00:17:30,287 --> 00:17:34,407
I met her here when I asked if I could work for her, and then she hired me.

337
00:17:34,527 --> 00:17:35,627
She didn't even think it over?

338
00:17:37,007 --> 00:17:38,067
This is suspicious.

339
00:17:38,787 --> 00:17:41,787
She's got to have some ulterior motive for wanting to work here so urgently.

340
00:17:41,987 --> 00:17:43,327
So, how can I help you today?

341
00:17:43,747 --> 00:17:44,707
Oh, right.

342
00:17:45,207 --> 00:17:47,207
This is yours. A uniform and apron.

343
00:17:47,787 --> 00:17:48,667
Things to wear?

344
00:17:49,207 --> 00:17:49,687
Fun!

345
00:17:49,687 --> 00:17:52,707
Cut it out!

346
00:17:52,827 --> 00:17:54,167
What's wrong with you, you perv?

347
00:17:54,547 --> 00:17:56,347
Oh, that's right. I forgot.

348
00:17:56,767 --> 00:17:57,987
You naughty boy.

349
00:17:58,607 --> 00:18:00,507
If you're sorry, keep your shirt on!

350
00:18:01,207 --> 00:18:02,587
You're all changing in the back.

351
00:18:02,727 --> 00:18:04,287
Oh, right. I understand.

352
00:18:05,367 --> 00:18:06,507
What the heck was that?

353
00:18:06,807 --> 00:18:08,487
Is she from a country with that kind of culture?

354
00:18:08,847 --> 00:18:09,967
I don't want to go there.

355
00:18:10,087 --> 00:18:10,787
Hey, Takito?

356
00:18:11,207 --> 00:18:12,387
Just Take's fine.

357
00:18:12,907 --> 00:18:13,587
What's the matter?

358
00:18:13,587 --> 00:18:16,127
I can't get the buttons on top to close.

359
00:18:17,027 --> 00:18:19,327
It's fine. You're fine. No one will notice.

360
00:18:19,467 --> 00:18:20,567
Oh, I get it.

361
00:18:21,127 --> 00:18:22,307
You're a pervert, huh?

362
00:18:23,207 --> 00:18:24,227
What'd you call me?

363
00:18:24,487 --> 00:18:24,967
You're staring.

364
00:18:25,787 --> 00:18:27,607
No, I'm not. They're in the way.

365
00:18:28,807 --> 00:18:29,707
I'll be in back.

366
00:18:29,907 --> 00:18:31,747
Let me know if there's anything you don't understand.

367
00:18:34,927 --> 00:18:36,787
She's a whole new breed of weirdo.

368
00:18:36,787 --> 00:18:40,967
I'm surprised Grandma decided to hire such a bizarre person.

369
00:18:42,427 --> 00:18:44,887
She makes less sense than someone with ulterior motives,

370
00:18:45,007 --> 00:18:45,707
and it's scary.

371
00:18:46,087 --> 00:18:47,567
Does she even know what she's doing?

372
00:18:48,007 --> 00:18:49,367
Can I have this, please?

373
00:18:49,447 --> 00:18:50,107
Sure thing.

374
00:18:50,487 --> 00:18:51,407
I want that.

375
00:18:52,387 --> 00:18:53,087
This one?

376
00:18:53,307 --> 00:18:53,627
Yeah.

377
00:18:54,367 --> 00:18:56,747
Do we sell these individually or as a set?

378
00:18:57,047 --> 00:18:58,347
We sell them both ways.

379
00:18:59,107 --> 00:19:01,227
Man, she's actually trying to do a good job.

380
00:19:02,887 --> 00:19:04,427
And she does more than I would have.

381
00:19:04,427 --> 00:19:06,627
I guess that's why Grandma decided to hire her.

382
00:19:06,787 --> 00:19:09,067
How come you have such big watermelons?

383
00:19:09,667 --> 00:19:11,027
Harassed on the first day?

384
00:19:11,247 --> 00:19:12,387
How will she handle it?

385
00:19:12,587 --> 00:19:14,447
These are actually called flame sacks.

386
00:19:14,607 --> 00:19:16,327
They're so strong they can hold fire.

387
00:19:16,447 --> 00:19:17,987
Whoa, that's cool.

388
00:19:18,007 --> 00:19:19,447
What kind of deflection was that?

389
00:19:19,987 --> 00:19:21,287
Do they hurt your back?

390
00:19:21,887 --> 00:19:22,607
Are they heavy?

391
00:19:24,387 --> 00:19:25,747
Would you like to hold them?

392
00:19:26,207 --> 00:19:27,627
Stop! What are you doing?

393
00:19:27,767 --> 00:19:28,687
Don't be weirdo!

394
00:19:28,687 --> 00:19:28,867
Ah!

395
00:19:35,107 --> 00:19:36,727
Poor Take, are you okay?

396
00:19:36,787 --> 00:19:39,307
I'm sorry!

397
00:19:40,247 --> 00:19:40,927
Uh-huh.

398
00:19:41,707 --> 00:19:43,707
It's okay, bad boy.

399
00:19:44,027 --> 00:19:45,687
What's with the delayed reactions?

400
00:19:47,607 --> 00:19:48,827
Bye-bye.

401
00:19:49,407 --> 00:19:49,767
Goodbye!

402
00:19:50,727 --> 00:19:52,027
You two have a good night!

403
00:19:52,027 --> 00:19:59,467
Want to know something?

404
00:20:00,187 --> 00:20:01,307
I like kids.

405
00:20:01,787 --> 00:20:02,967
They're fun to play with.

406
00:20:03,247 --> 00:20:03,467
Hmm?

407
00:20:04,747 --> 00:20:06,967
But I'm not allowed to play with them while I'm working.

408
00:20:07,687 --> 00:20:10,967
I thought if I worked somewhere where there were children, it would be more fun.

409
00:20:10,967 --> 00:20:18,407
It's time for us to close up shop for the night.

410
00:20:19,867 --> 00:20:21,127
Maybe we could play together.

411
00:20:21,367 --> 00:20:23,027
I'll show you how to spin a top if you want.

412
00:20:23,107 --> 00:20:24,067
It's actually pretty easy.

413
00:20:24,067 --> 00:20:25,287
Oh, yeah, that!

414
00:20:25,447 --> 00:20:26,567
I'm dying to learn!

415
00:20:26,707 --> 00:20:27,447
I'll go get it!

416
00:20:28,087 --> 00:20:29,107
She's a nice girl.

417
00:20:29,667 --> 00:20:31,467
Looks like I won't have to worry about Grandma.

418
00:20:33,467 --> 00:20:34,187
Hey, Take.

419
00:20:34,507 --> 00:20:35,607
I think I like you.

420
00:20:35,667 --> 00:20:36,967
Who's that supposed to say that?

421
00:20:37,027 --> 00:20:37,967
After Kobayashi.

422
00:20:38,927 --> 00:20:39,987
And who's that?

423
00:20:40,627 --> 00:20:41,307
Kobo what?

424
00:20:42,247 --> 00:20:43,227
Here it is.

425
00:20:44,327 --> 00:20:45,407
Watch closely.

426
00:20:51,967 --> 00:20:53,487
Want to hear something interesting?

427
00:20:53,947 --> 00:20:56,087
Apparently, humans make wishes on stars.

428
00:20:56,387 --> 00:20:56,947
Did you know that?

429
00:20:57,507 --> 00:20:57,827
Huh?

430
00:20:58,307 --> 00:21:01,087
They pray to the stars for peace and happiness.

431
00:21:01,807 --> 00:21:05,447
Or bountiful harvests, or health for themselves, their friends and families.

432
00:21:06,427 --> 00:21:07,787
Sounds like they don't care.

433
00:21:07,967 --> 00:21:10,587
Who grants their wishes, as long as they're fulfilled.

434
00:21:11,147 --> 00:21:13,047
What an utterly inferior species.

435
00:21:14,207 --> 00:21:16,167
And what would you wish for, Toru?

436
00:21:16,407 --> 00:21:18,467
If your wish was guaranteed to come true?

437
00:21:22,867 --> 00:21:23,807
Nothing, really.

438
00:21:26,867 --> 00:21:27,907
I'd make a wish.

439
00:21:28,087 --> 00:21:29,307
Oh, I'm sure you would.

440
00:21:29,447 --> 00:21:31,327
All the yummy sweets in the world, that right?

441
00:21:32,627 --> 00:21:34,267
You do know me quite well.

442
00:21:35,407 --> 00:21:36,367
You're close.

443
00:21:36,587 --> 00:21:37,807
But no, that's not it.

444
00:21:37,967 --> 00:21:38,727
What then?

445
00:21:39,167 --> 00:21:42,867
I'm going to have all the delicious food, and then I'm going to have your share, too.

446
00:21:43,087 --> 00:21:43,287
Oh.

447
00:21:48,147 --> 00:21:49,147
As you wish.

448
00:23:19,967 --> 00:23:21,967
Our lunch break is way too short.

449
00:23:21,967 --> 00:23:23,967
Don't you agree, Ms. Kobayashi?

450
00:23:23,967 --> 00:23:25,967
Not really, no.

451
00:23:25,967 --> 00:23:27,967
There are five places on my current list

452
00:23:27,967 --> 00:23:29,967
that I really want to try for lunch,

453
00:23:29,967 --> 00:23:31,967
but I only have enough time to hit two of them.

454
00:23:31,967 --> 00:23:33,967
Most people only go to one.

455
00:23:33,967 --> 00:23:35,967
I'm hungry, okay?

456
00:23:35,967 --> 00:23:37,967
This week on Who's Rotten?

457
00:23:37,967 --> 00:23:39,967
Capricorn.

